- \( UFL_i \) is the UFL of component \( i \).
- \( w_i \) is the mass fraction of component \( i \) in the mixture.

This equation is derived from the **thermorilic law**, which states that the total volume of gases in a mixture is equal to the sum of the partial volumes of the individual components.

