","The addition of silicon doping to TiO2 nanoparticles, such as in the synthesis of TiO2 nanotubes, can significantly affect the sintering process and grain size distribution. Here are some of the effects:

1. Si doping can lead to the formation of Si-O-Ti bonds, which can act as a liquid phase during sintering. This liquid phase lowers the viscosity of the material, promoting grain boundary diffusion and promoting sintering at lower temperatures and for better density.

2. The presence of Si can also affect the surface energy of the nanoparticles, which in turn can influence the grain size during sintering.

