$$\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \frac{s_1^3}{s_2^3} = \left(\frac{s_1}{s_2}\right)^3 = \left(\frac{3}{1}\right)^3 = 27$
Thus, the ratio of the volumes is 27:1. Since the volume of the first cube is 27, the volume of the second cube is:
$$\frac{27}{V_2} = \frac{27}{1} \implies V_2 = 1$

