","The maximum frequency shift in the Compton scattering is given by:
\[
\Delta \lambda_{\text{max}} = \lambda_{\text{scatter}} - \lambda_{\text{incident}} = \lambda_{\text{Compontes}}
\]
The Compton scattering formula is:
\[
\lambda_{\text{scatter}} = \lambda_{\text{incident}} \left( \frac{1}{1 - \frac{\hbar \omega}{m_e c^2}} \right)
\]
The maximum wavelength shift occurs when the scattering angle is \(\theta = 180^\circ\). Substituting \(\theta = 180^\circ\) into the Compton scattering formula:
\[
\lambda_{\text{scatter}} = \lambda_{\text{incident}} \left( \frac{1}{1 - \frac{\hbar \omega}{m_e c^2}} \right)
\]
For \(\theta = 180^\circ\), the angle between the incident and scattered photons is \(\theta = 180^\circ\), and the original and scattered photons pass opposite directions. The original photon loses all its energy to the electron, which is at rest. The energy of the photon is:
\[
\varepsilon = \frac{\hbar \omega}{c} = \frac{hc}{\lambda_{\text{incident}}}
\]
Substituting this into the Compton scattering formula:
\[
\lambda_{\text{scatter}} = \lambda_{\text{incident}} \left( \frac{1}{1 - \frac{\hbar \omega}{m_e c^2}} \right) = \lambda_{\text{incident}} \left( \frac{1}{1 - \frac{hc}{c \lambda_{\text{incident}} m_e c^2}} \right) = \lambda_{\text{incident}} \left( \frac{1}{1 - \frac{\lambda_{\text{incident}}}{m_e c^2 \lambda_{\text{incident}}} \lambda_{\text{incident}}} \right)
\]
\[
\lambda_{\text{scatter}} = \lambda_{\text{incident}} \left( \frac{1}{1 - \frac{1}{m_e c^2}} \right)
\]
Substituting the values:
\[
m_e = 9.109 \times 10^{-31} \text{ kg}
\]
\[
c = 2.998 \times 10^8 \text{ m/s}
\]
\[
m_e c^2 = 9.109 \times 10^{-31} \times (2.998 \times 10^8)^2 = 8.187 \times 10^{-14} \text{ J} = 0.511 \text{ MeV}
\]
\[
\lambda_{\text{scatter}} = \lambda_{\text{incident}} \left( \frac{1}{1 - \frac{1}{0.511 \text{ MeV}}} \right)
\]
The energy of the photon is \(2.00 \text{ Å} = 2.00 \times 10^{-10} \text{ m}\). The energy of the photon is:
\[
\boxed{E} = \frac{hc}{\lambda} = \frac{6.626 \times 10^{-34} \times 2.998 \times 10^8}{2.00",relevance,"# Task Description
