</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
(a) The force on the proton due to the electric field is \(F = qE\), where \(q = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C}\) and \(E = 500 \, \text{N/C}\). The force is:  
\[ F = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C})(500 \, \text{N/C}) = 8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N} \]  
Using Newton's second law, \(F = ma\), we find the acceleration:  
\[ a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} \approx 4.79 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2 \]  

