E = 150 \times \left(1 - 0.7143\right)
\]
\[
E = 150 \times 0.2857 = 42.855 \, \text{J}
\]

**Step 2: Calculate the total energy released by HMTD**
\[
E_{\text{total}} = \frac{42.855 \, \text{J}}{0.7} = 61.22 \, \text{J}
\]

**Step 3: Calculate the mass of TNT equivalent to the energy released by HMTD**
\[
\text{Mass of TNT} = \frac{61.22 \, \text{J}}{4680 \, \text{J/g}} = 0.0131 \, \text{g}
